00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
the cold war saw two sides face off in  an ideological battle for the future  in europe and north america the conflict  is often discussed as being between nato  and the warsaw pact  but nato predates the warsaw pact by six  years and during that six years  something interesting happened the ussr  asked to join  which raises a pretty obvious question  why why did the ussr want to join nato  so in the four years prior to the  establishment of nato the ussr and the  western powers had a pretty rocky  relationship  the west was extremely concerned with  the red army given that it was  absolutely massive and there were  worries in washington that the ussr may  start conquering territory piecemeal and  pick off the western countries one by  one  as such the western powers founded nato  the north atlantic treaty organization  to protect themselves from any potential  threats in the future  now officially this was a simple  defensive alliance that anyone in europe  could be a member of and wasn't aimed  specifically at any one nation  unofficially though it was the communist  scary club now the soviets weren't silly  and its leadership was at this point  filled with pretty shrewd diplomats who  knew what nato really was  and when stalin opted to follow in  lenin's footsteps and die there was a  chance for the ussr's foreign policy to  pivot  two people important to this were  lavrenty beria and viator slav molotov  who came up with an interesting idea  let's make friends with the west this  plan involved several steps  the first was the reunification of  germany on the condition that had become  a perpetually neutral state  in return for what was essentially the  ussr giving up east germany the leaders  of which were not consulted the soviet  union wanted to join the new european  defense community which as the name  suggests didn't include any  non-europeans  obviously the western powers would never  go along with this and so when it was  rejected to make it look like they were  conceding something the soviets offered  to join nato  this offer was semi-serious in that the  soviet leadership expected it to be  rejected but prepared for the  eventuality that the western leadership  would get very drunk or something and  say yes  so why did they apply to join well the  answer is simple  it was a win-win if the western powers  rejected soviet membership then they  were admitting that nato was in fact an  anti-soviet bloc which would in turn  allow the ussr to build its own alliance  and give it much greater free reign in  its foreign policy  if the western powers accepted soviet  membership the nato's character as an  anti-soviet alliance would change into a  general european defensive one and also  germany would stay forever disarmed  which given recent events was something  that the ussr very much wanted  as you'll be aware the answer from the  west was a no not for want of churchill  trying and the no was for the exact same  reasons that the ussr wanted to join  however they weren't so open about the  exact reason why and cited the ussr's  non-democratic government and occupation  of eastern european nations for the  negative response  and so the ussr was now free to act in  retaliation and did so by forming its  own alliance in 1955 and thus  the warsaw pact was born i hope you  enjoyed this episode and thank you for  watching with a special thanks to my  patrons  james bissonette kelly moneymaker rob  waterhouse moe  marvin cassell aaron the white jordan  longley james castaneda gustav swann  jerry landon  maggie patzkowski copper tone rasheed  ali winston caywood misses it  spinning three plates lexi schwinn  matthew shipley anthony beckett robert  wetzel  marcus arsenault corso wolf spencer  lightfoot and charles the first
 

